<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shankaragana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 575–600</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shankaragana was a king of the Kalachuris of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahishmati">Mahishmati</a> in the late 6th century, son of Krishnaraja and father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddharaja">Buddharaja</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">Copper</a>-plate grants show his authority reaching <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ujjain">Ujjain</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>. The dynasty's power declined soon after his reign under pressure from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badami">Badami</a>.</p></div>
